Z||000000||SloPonti||10-20-1999||12:46 AM||||tonight i was drinving on the highway and she just quit!! i think she made a slight popping noise but am not for sure! i pulled over and tried to start again but no start-l then listened for the fuel pump and it was running! i got out and did some simple checks and still no go so i got out my tools and pulled a spark plug and the car has no spark-so i check all fuses and they were good and i pulled the codes and got a code 12! i then went to the parts store and a bought a new coil and ignition module-which i then replaced and still not working! the motor turns over fine but no spark! wires are fine and spark plugs are new! last summer i replaced the computer and a new fuel pump has been add a couple of months ago! i checked the wires on the coil and when the key is on i have power on all four wires! i then traced the wires to the distribiter and there is power going to there so i don't think there are any broken wires! if anyone can help that would be great! someone has to help me get her back on the road!!!!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||9
Z||000001||lowCG||10-20-1999||01:34 AM||||Did you check the grounds?<BR>Need both sides to do it(+,-),just a thought.<BR>Is there power to the coil when you're cranking it as well as when the key is on?||||reg||1
Z||000002||mwbackus||10-20-1999||02:46 AM||||Just a note :  When checking for trouble codes you will always get a code 12, this is the indication that the ECM is receiving reference pulses like it should.  After code 12 flashes 3 times, the actual trouble codes will flash if any are present.  <BR>     It sounds alot like the pickup coil. How did it look when you replaced the module?<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000003||ka4nkf||10-20-1999||04:00 AM||||My Vote Is For The Pick Up Coil||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||10-20-1999||09:53 AM||||did you check to make sure the distributor is turning? if you scarfed a cam gear it would do about the same thing.<P>otherwise,,, the pickup is the only thing cheap left..... ||||reg||1
